WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.080
The Red Woman Melisandre has uttered many
memorable lines throughout Game of Thrones

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.080
history.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.110
"Death is coming for everyone and everything.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.440
A darkness that will swallow the dawn."

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.880
Fans can always count on the mystical priestess
to deliver powerful truths while propagating

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:19.040
her faith in the Lord of Light and changing
the lives of many - for better and for worse.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.520
One such Westerosi whom Melisandre has crossed
paths with is Arya Stark, and on the latest

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.520
episode of Game of Thrones, the two women
had a conversation that has ignited a fascinating

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.170
theory about where the series will go from
here.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.030
Just before Arya takes a flying leap at the
Night King and kills him with her Valyrian

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:38.180
steel dagger, and just after Beric bravely
sacrifices his life to save Arya's as she's

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:41.870
overwhelmed by wights in the corridors of
Winterfell, she meets with Melisandre for

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.000
a mid-battle chat.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.110
This isn't the first time Melisandre and Arya
have spoken: the first encounter they had

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:51.280
was on the third season of Thrones, when Melisandre
prophesied Arya's future.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.430
“Brown eyes, blue eyes, green eyes.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.110
Eyes you'll shut forever.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.630
We will meet again."

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:04.110
Arya did indeed shut many eyes forever before
finally slaughtering the Night King, a move

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.060
which also killed his entire army.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.520
When she and Melisandre met again, Arya confirmed
that the priestess can actually see the future.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.710
"You said I'd shut many eyes forever.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.200
You were right about that too."

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.000
"Brown eyes.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.670
Green eyes.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:19.729
And blue eyes."

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:23.770
Off Arya went to kill the blue-eyed Night
King, thus sealing shut her second set of

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:24.770
eyes.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.890
But what about the third eye color Melisandre
mentioned?

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:31.130
Many fans believe that those green eyes belong
to none other than Cersei Lannister and that

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.960
Arya will murder the Mad Queen when she and
the survivors of the Battle of Winterfell

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.049
arrive in King's Landing on the next episode
of Game of Thrones.

00:01:37.049 --> 00:01:41.750
Cersei's eyes are definitely green, described
by author George R.R. Martin as a perfect

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.460
match to the emeralds of a tiara she once
wore.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.460
Actress Lena Headey, too, has green eyes.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:50.759
However, astute fans will recall that Arya
has already killed someone with green eyes:

00:01:50.759 --> 00:01:51.759
Littlefinger.

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:55.390
His peepers are said to be gray-green and
cat-like in Martin's A Song of Ice and Fire

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:58.680
book series, though actor Aiden Gillen's eyes
are blue in real life.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:03.040
If Arya does have more green eyes to close,
will she actually kill the emerald-eyed Cersei?

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.830
The Mad Queen is one of a few names left on
Arya's hit list, standing with the Hound and

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:10.940
the Mountain, so there's not exactly a lack
of desire to murder her on Arya's part.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.680
There's also a strong chance that Arya might
murder Jaime Lannister, Cersei's twin who

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.120
shares her eye color, then implement the techniques
she learned at the House of Black and White

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.670
in Braavos to disguise herself as Jaime and
kill Cersei.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:25.900
Such an act would connect to another major
Game of Thrones prophecy: the one Cersei received

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:26.900
in her youth.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.930
In a Season 5 flashback, fortune teller Maggy
the Frog told Cersei that she would marry

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:35.599
a king, he would father 20 children and she
would give birth to three, and her children

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:38.520
would each taste power before dying while
she was still alive.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.629
In Martin's novels, the conversation continues,
and Maggy tells Cersei that she will eventually

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.300
be overcome with grief and pain.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:49.240
At that time, she will be murdered by a Valonqar
- the word for "little brother" in High Valyrian.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:52.830
Cersei's other sibling Tyrion could be the
little brother who murders her, especially

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.620
given that he's bent the knee to Daenerys.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:58.660
However, "valonqar" means little brother and
not littlest, meaning that Jaime, who was

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:02.650
born minutes after Cersei, could also be the
one to kill her, or at least someone who looks

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:03.650
just like him.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:07.250
Arya stealing Jaime's face to do the deed
would be a surprise twist for viewers, and

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:10.760
might even link up to Maggy's mention that
a "younger and more beautiful" queen will

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.599
cast Cersei down and take all that she holds
dear.

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:17.420
Perhaps Daenerys will be the one to ask Arya
to murder Jaime as revenge for the Lannister

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.780
man slaying her father during Robert's Rebellion.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:24.700
Then, Arya might snatch Jaime's mug, fulfill
Maggy's prophecy by murdering Cersei as Jaime,

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.930
and clear the Iron Throne for Daenerys to
take.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:31.069
Since few predicted that Arya would even kill
the Night King on the latest episode, there

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:35.010
really is no saying how sound these theories
are or anticipating what exactly will happen

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.010
next.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:39.610
Hopefully, the next episode of Game of Thrones
will clear up any lingering questions about

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:44.510
Arya and Melisandre's conversation and reveal
whether Cersei will live to see another day.

